WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.584
It's reported at least 44 trans
people were murdered

00:00:02.626 --> 00:00:07.042
in 2020 alone,
and despite your fears, you say

00:00:07.083 --> 00:00:12.375
you feel a deep responsibility
to share your truth.

00:00:12.417 --> 00:00:15.626
Why?

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:19.417
Well, you know, so much of
the privilege I have,

00:00:19.459 --> 00:00:24.292
the ability to be here
sitting here right now

00:00:24.334 --> 00:00:27.083
is really because of so many
trans women of color

00:00:27.125 --> 00:00:30.125
who have consistently
put their lives on the line

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:31.709
throughout history, you know?

00:00:31.751 --> 00:00:36.959
When we think of
Marsha P. Johnson or Miss Major.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.375
I'm grateful to have the access
to the resources I've had

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:45.083
because I don't know what
would have happened if I didn't.

00:00:45.125 --> 00:00:48.000
And there's so many people
in this community, like I said,

00:00:48.042 --> 00:00:50.125
don't have access
to health care already

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:52.792
and then you have now in states

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.876
that are trying to ban
gender-affirming health care

00:00:55.918 --> 00:00:57.876
for transgender youth,

00:00:57.918 --> 00:01:01.459
and I guess I don't know how to
really say it

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:05.417
other than it just feels
more important

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.918
than feeling scared
in moments.

00:01:07.959 --> 00:01:12.459
It feels more important than if
I have an overwhelming day.

00:01:14.292 --> 00:01:17.375
It, to me, really simply feels

00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:19.918
like absolutely
the right thing to do.

00:01:19.959 --> 00:01:24.792
Who or what force helped you
to move through the fear?

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.918
Who did you lean on
or what did you lean on

00:01:27.959 --> 00:01:31.292
to help you move
through the fear?

00:01:31.334 --> 00:01:35.209
I'm surrounded by
really incredible people

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.709
who I work with
and just fully support me.

00:01:38.751 --> 00:01:42.167
Friends who, you know,
fully support me

00:01:42.209 --> 00:01:45.667
and are there for me.
And, um, and again,

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:48.334
being inspired by
so many people

00:01:48.375 --> 00:01:53.334
who have a lot more courage
that I do and that, you know,

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:57.417
that love and support
and encouragement.

00:01:57.459 --> 00:02:01.292
Was your mom-- was your mom
a big source of support?

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:05.042
Yeah, I mean, I-- I think as I
talked in the "Time" article,

00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:09.250
obviously in my childhood
and things were, you know,

00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:12.292
a bit different,
but my mom can't be, you know,

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:16.167
couldn't be more supportive
and such an advocate

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:18.709
for the LGBTQ+ community.

00:02:18.751 --> 00:02:23.667
So thrilled for me and that
I'm in this place in my life.

